<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AA124020003">
<title>
System Description
</title>
<ptxt>
When RBS control module judges that the system impairs the original performance, RBS control module suspends adaptive cruise control, and outputs DTC C1640. However, when the cause of the suspension is eliminated, RBS control module turns off adaptive cruise control warning light, clears the DTC and resumes the system function automatically.
</ptxt>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AA124020004">
<title>
DTC Confirmation Procedure
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition “ON”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AA124020005">
<title>
DTC Troubleshooting
</title>
<attention3>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
DTC C1640 can be detected as a current DTC but it is not stored as a history DTC.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
When any malfunction is detected on each parameter in the following table, “NG” indication is maintained. Therefore, after resuming the system to be normal, the factor of the malfunction can be checked in “Data List” of SUZUKI scan tool. The “NG” indication is maintained until the DTC is cleared.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check each parameter in the table below using SUZUKI scan tool.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Diagnose the defective parameter according to diagnosis flow. If diagnosis flow does not correspond to the parameter, perform 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA124001">Adaptive Cruise Control System Check:Adaptive Cruise Control</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</s1>
